From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] block: dispatch HFS filesystem checks to hfsprogs

HFS and HFS+ volumes have no checker dispatch even when filesystem checking
is enabled and hfsprogs is installed. Select its fsck.hfsplus binary for both
probe types and use the existing noninteractive -p invocation.

Keep checker absence and failure handling unchanged. This dispatch neither
enables filesystem checking nor installs the optional checker.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
---

--- a/block.c
+++ b/block.c
@@ -775,6 +775,7 @@
 	const char *fatfsck = "/usr/sbin/fsck.fat";
 	const char *btrfsck = "/usr/bin/btrfsck";
 	const char *ntfsck = "/usr/bin/ntfsfix";
+	const char *hfsck = "/usr/sbin/fsck.hfsplus";
 	const char *ckfs;
 
 	/* UBIFS does not need stuff like fsck */
@@ -791,6 +792,8 @@
 		ckfs = btrfsck;
 	} else if (!strncmp(pr->type, "ntfs", 4)) {
 		ckfs = ntfsck;
+	} else if (!strcmp(pr->type, "hfs") || !strcmp(pr->type, "hfsplus")) {
+		ckfs = hfsck;
 	} else {
 		ULOG_ERR("check_filesystem: %s is not supported\n", pr->type);
 		return;
